## 1470. Shuffle the Array

## Approach
- The array contains two halves: first half has x values and second half has y values.
- For every index i:
  - Take x from nums[i].
  - Take y from nums[n + i].
- Put x at position 2 * i in the new array.
- Put y at position 2 * i + 1.
- Continue until all n pairs are added.

## Complexity

- Time: O(n)
- Space: O(n), because it uses an extra array.

SOLUTION:
class Solution {
    public int[] shuffle(int[] nums, int n) {
        int[] newArr = new int[2 * n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            newArr[2 * i] = nums[i];
            newArr[2 * i + 1] = nums[n + i];
        }
        return newArr;
    }
}
